From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Rob Vogelaar <rob.vogelaar@example.com>
Date: Wed, 2 Sep 2026 16:45:00 -0700
Subject: [PATCH] controller: scope BSS list deletion to matching radio

The database BSS delete path evaluates the operation criteria before
deleting a row, but it unconditionally removes every visited BSS from the
controller's in-memory list.  A radio-scoped delete therefore empties the
global model and a subsequent reconciliation makes that loss persistent.
This is especially visible after a controller restart, when the colocated
agent's ten tri-band BSS records collapse to a partial set.

Apply the same match result to both representations so the in-memory model
and database remain consistent and unrelated radios are preserved.

Upstream-Status: Pending
Signed-off-by: Rob Vogelaar <rob.vogelaar@example.com>
---
 src/ctrl/dm_easy_mesh_ctrl.cpp | 12 +++++++-----
 1 file changed, 7 insertions(+), 5 deletions(-)

diff --git a/src/ctrl/dm_easy_mesh_ctrl.cpp b/src/ctrl/dm_easy_mesh_ctrl.cpp
index 1111111..2222222 100644
--- a/src/ctrl/dm_easy_mesh_ctrl.cpp
+++ b/src/ctrl/dm_easy_mesh_ctrl.cpp
@@ -4749,11 +4749,13 @@ int dm_easy_mesh_ctrl_t::update_tables(dm_easy_mesh_t *dm)
         for (i = 0; i < dm->get_num_bss(); i++) {
             bss = dm->get_bss_by_ref(i);
 			criteria = dm->db_cfg_type_get_criteria(db_cfg_type_bss_list_delete);
-			if ((bss.match_criteria(criteria) == true) && (dm->get_bss(i)) &&
-					(dm_bss_list_t::update_db(m_db_client, dm_orch_type_db_delete, dm->get_bss(i)->get_bss_info()) != 0)) {
-                at_least_one_failed = true;
-            }
-			dm_bss_list_t::update_list(bss, dm_orch_type_db_delete);
+			if ((bss.match_criteria(criteria) == true) && (dm->get_bss(i))) {
+				if (dm_bss_list_t::update_db(m_db_client, dm_orch_type_db_delete,
+						dm->get_bss(i)->get_bss_info()) != 0) {
+					at_least_one_failed = true;
+				}
+				dm_bss_list_t::update_list(bss, dm_orch_type_db_delete);
+			}
         }
         if (at_least_one_failed == true) {
             at_least_one_failed = false;
